---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, SOCIALS } from '../consts';

---

<Base
    title="About"
    description="Jenish Kothari. Software Engineer II at Adobe, MS CS Northeastern. Post-training, small local models, and execution-verified evaluation."
>
    <article>
        <h1>About</h1>

        <p>
            I'm Jenish Kothari. Software Engineer II at <strong>Adobe</strong> in
            Salt Lake City, and an MS CS graduate of <strong>Northeastern
            University</strong> (2026). Before that, BS Computer Science at Nirma
            University.
        </p>

        <p>
            My work is post-training: SFT, reasoning distillation, DPO, and GRPO.
            At Adobe I distilled a production LLM down to a 3B parameter model,
            cutting inference cost 10&times; while holding 72% of GPT-4 benchmarks.
            Outside work I'm doing the same for text-to-SQL in the open, in a
            series called <a href="/post-training-101/">Post-Training 101</a>.
        </p>

        <p>
            I care most about small models that run locally: one GPU, no API bill.
            See <a href="/projects/">Projects</a> for the numbers.
        </p>

        <h2>Experience</h2>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr><th>Where</th><th>Role</th><th>When</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Adobe</strong></td>
                    <td>Software Engineer II &middot; Salt Lake City, UT</td>
                    <td>Jun 2026 &ndash; present</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Dell Technologies</strong></td>
                    <td>Software Engineer Intern &middot; Boston, MA</td>
                    <td>Aug 2025 &ndash; Dec 2025</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Adobe</strong></td>
                    <td>Software Engineer Intern &middot; Salt Lake City, UT</td>
                    <td>May 2025 &ndash; Aug 2025</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>ZS Associates</strong></td>
                    <td>Software Engineer &middot; Pune, India</td>
                    <td>Aug 2022 &ndash; Dec 2023</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>
            Recent platform work: migrated access control for 5,000+ approval
            templates from MongoDB to a Zanzibar-style AuthZ service with a phased
            backfill and zero-downtime cutover, plus an automated reconciliation
            audit that caught orphaned templates from partial-failure edge cases
            before they reached customers.
        </p>

        <p>
            Published at <strong>IEEE ICAD 2026</strong>. Won the
            <a href="https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/build-with-gemma-justbuild"
                >Build with Gemma</a
            > hackathon (Kaggle &times; <a href="https://justbuild.ing">JustBuild</a>),
            the Confluent Kafka hackathon, and Best Project at the Harvard AI
            Hackathon. Mostly Python and PyTorch, with whatever else the problem
            needs.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
            Most responsive on <a href={SOCIALS.x}>X DMs</a>. Email:
            <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Also on
            <a href={SOCIALS.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>,
            <a href={SOCIALS.github}>GitHub</a>,
            <a href={SOCIALS.huggingface}>Hugging Face</a>, and
            <a href={SOCIALS.kaggle}>Kaggle</a>.
        </p>
    </article>
</Base>
